        meaning: "whose / from where / which language",
        explanation: "Three small tools for talking about a person. (1) の links a person to their company or study: そらの かいしゃいん = 'a Sora company employee', 日本語の がくせい = 'a student of Japanese' — the group comes first. (2) 〜人 turns a country into a nationality: アメリカ → アメリカ人, 日本 → 日本人. (3) 〜語 makes a language: 日本語 (Japanese), えいご (English), スペイン語 (Spanish). To ask, use the question word 何: 何人ですか (which nationality?), 何語ですか (which language?).",
