    order: 5,
    recap: "Last week you learned to point and pay — ここ, そこ, いくらですか, これを ください. You can find the shop and buy the cake. Tonight you get the other half of every plan: what time, and from when until when.",
    intro: "Japanese tells the time in a tidy, friendly way. The hour is 〜じ, the minutes are 〜ふん, and に means 'at'. Then two little words — から (from) and まで (until) — stretch one time into a whole afternoon. We'll build a real daily schedule with them, and keep an eye on two hiragana shapes that trip everyone up: the stretched long vowel and the tiny っ.",
