        explanation: "Say the hour with 〜じ and the minutes with 〜ふん (it voices to 〜ぷん after some numbers). To say you do something AT that time, add に after it: しちじに おきます, 'I get up at seven'. はん means 'half past' (くじはん = 9:30). ごぜん is a.m., ごご is p.m. A few readings change shape and are worth learning by ear: よじ (4:00), しちじ (7:00), くじ (9:00). Written out, the hour is usually the kanji 時 and the minutes 分 — tonight we read them in kana so you can hear them.",
