    order: 5,
    recap: "Lesson 7 used 〜とか to offer examples and んです to explain a situation before a request. This pre-study lesson turns one of those examples into a decision: what shall we actually do?",
    intro: "The volitional form is compact but systematic. Godan verbs move one vowel, ichidan verbs take よう, and only する and 来る need special attention. Once you can hear the long おう, your first intention sentence is already within reach.",
